          "children": [
            {
              "id": "22df80e2-6795-445e-b0c5-a6c381ba8e50",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>Gods &amp; Games: Toward a Theology of Play</strong></em> was written by David L. Miller, originally published by The World Publishing Company in 1970."
            },
            {
              "id": "20da5a06-3200-4c96-af0b-ba8763ba292f",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "8443e30a-ad9b-4e28-afc9-7e5d91907df3",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>A deeply thoughtful, deeply irreverent look at the mythology of play </em>Gods &amp; Games<em> ties together </em><a href=\"#/the-masks-of-god\"><em>Joseph Campbell's approach to myth</em></a><em> and religion with </em><a href=\"#/johan-huizinga\"><em>Johan Huizinga</em></a><em>'s view of our species as </em><a href=\"#/homo-ludens-44772672\"><em>Homo ludens</em></a><em> — &quot;Man the Game-player&quot; — which suggests that play is a central aspect of the human spirit and human culture.</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "78e63908-630f-4928-8944-ad73145e6bc7",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "a0e5e97b-3c83-49a4-b711-0ff4768f2a93",
              "type": "paragraph",
